# Powers GitHub's "Cite this repository" button. Releases are versioned at build time only (the repo
# stays at 0.0.0-dev), so no version is stored here: cite the version shown in your export.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tramus in your research, please cite it as below and state the exact version you used (Settings → About, or any export)."
type: software
title: Tramus
abstract: "Tramus tracks a single mouse in top-down lab videos and measures time in user-drawn zones. Free, open source, runs offline on Windows, macOS and Linux."
authors:
  - name: "The Tramus contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/advename/tramus"
url: "https://advename.github.io/tramus/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - behavioral neuroscience
  - mouse tracking
  - animal behavior
  - time in zone
  - three-chamber test
  - open field
  - computer vision
